From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] touchpanel_mtdev: fix finger type and declare the gesture
 helpers

The mtdev touchpanel module does not build with GCC 15, which defaults to
-std=gnu23 and so rejects implicit function declarations outright:

    touchpanel.c:661: error: implicit declaration of function 'add_new_finger'
    touchpanel.c:668: error: implicit declaration of function 'update_finger'
    touchpanel.c:681: error: implicit declaration of function
                            'gesture_state_machine_process'

All three are defined in touchpanel_gestures.c but were never declared in
touchpanel_gestures.h, because gesture_state_machine() is the only entry point
the header was written for. touchpanel.c drives the slot bookkeeping itself and
calls the three helpers directly, so declare them.

That in turn exposes the type mt_slot_t was using to hold a finger:

    touchpanel.c:661: error: assignment to 'struct finger_t *' from 'int'
                            makes pointer from integer without a cast

touchpanel_gestures.h declares "typedef struct finger { ... } finger_t;", so
the struct tag is "finger" and "struct finger_t" is a different, never-defined
type. It compiled only because nothing checked it: the member was assigned from
an implicitly-declared function returning int, and passed to another one taking
no declared parameter types. Use finger_t, and initialise the member to NULL
rather than -1 - the reset loop was the odd one out, the teardown path at line
670 already uses NULL.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/touchpanel_mtdev/touchpanel.c          |  4 ++--
 src/touchpanel_mtdev/touchpanel_gestures.h |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/touchpanel_mtdev/touchpanel.c
+++ b/src/touchpanel_mtdev/touchpanel.c
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@
 	int posY;
 	int tracking_id;
 	int previous_tracking_id;
-	struct finger_t *nyx_finger;
+	finger_t *nyx_finger;
 } mt_slot_t;
 struct mtdev *ts_mtdev = NULL;
 /*
@@ -444,7 +444,7 @@
         {
             mt_slots[iSlot].tracking_id = -1;
             mt_slots[iSlot].previous_tracking_id = -1;
-            mt_slots[iSlot].nyx_finger = -1;
+            mt_slots[iSlot].nyx_finger = NULL;
         }
     }
 
--- a/src/touchpanel_mtdev/touchpanel_gestures.h
+++ b/src/touchpanel_mtdev/touchpanel_gestures.h
@@ -130,4 +130,13 @@
                            int fingerCount, const time_stamp_t *pTime,
                            input_event_t *events, int *numEvents);
 
+/* Used by the mtdev slot handling in touchpanel.c, which tracks the fingers
+   itself instead of going through gesture_state_machine(). */
+finger_t *add_new_finger(int x, int y, int weight,
+                         const time_stamp_t *pCurTime);
+void update_finger(finger_t *finger, int x, int y, int weight,
+                   const time_stamp_t *pCurTime);
+void gesture_state_machine_process(const time_stamp_t *pCurTime,
+                                   input_event_t *events, int *numEvents);
+
 #endif  /* __TOUCHPANEL_GESTURES_PRV_H */
